WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.288 --> 00:00:01.799
- Good morning believe nation, it's Evan.

00:00:01.799 --> 00:00:04.282
My one word is believe
and I believe that you

00:00:04.282 --> 00:00:06.562
have something special
that when you unleash it

00:00:06.562 --> 00:00:08.869
it will be able to change the world.

00:00:08.869 --> 00:00:11.116
So to help you on your
journey today's message is

00:00:11.116 --> 00:00:11.949
work hard.

00:00:12.984 --> 00:00:14.470
Over to you James Hedfield.

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:16.792
(rooster crows)

00:00:16.792 --> 00:00:19.421
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:19.421 --> 00:00:22.150
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:26.201
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:26.201 --> 00:00:29.701
- Most things in life that are worthwhile,

00:00:30.978 --> 00:00:32.028
you got to work at it.

00:00:32.028 --> 00:00:33.105
You got to work at.

00:00:33.105 --> 00:00:34.931
You get out what you put in.

00:00:34.931 --> 00:00:35.801
It's simple as that.

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:37.884
That's a kind of a universal law.

00:00:37.884 --> 00:00:41.717
So yeah, it's not pick
up the guitar and go

00:00:41.717 --> 00:00:44.985
ha, ha, which I've done, you know,

00:00:44.985 --> 00:00:46.581
in front of the mirror lots, you know.

00:00:46.581 --> 00:00:48.601
Hey, I'm really good and

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:50.407
you got to have that attitude too.

00:00:50.407 --> 00:00:52.641
But it does take work, it does take

00:00:52.641 --> 00:00:54.999
you know, some dedication, you know.

00:00:54.999 --> 00:00:58.742
But if you love doing
it, it's not as hard as

00:00:58.742 --> 00:01:01.236
it could be if you're doing something

00:01:01.236 --> 00:01:03.448
that you're not as interested in.

00:01:03.448 --> 00:01:05.911
- So on this channel we've
covered more successful

00:01:05.911 --> 00:01:09.395
people maybe than any
other channel on YouTube.

00:01:09.395 --> 00:01:11.131
I'd put it up against a lot of other

00:01:11.131 --> 00:01:12.826
internet properties just in general.

00:01:12.826 --> 00:01:14.915
We've covered entrepreneurs and athletes

00:01:14.915 --> 00:01:17.272
and musicians and
innovators and politicians

00:01:17.272 --> 00:01:20.330
and people who've had success
from all walks of life.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:23.396
And one of the most consistent
themes that come up,

00:01:23.396 --> 00:01:24.900
is you need to work hard.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.186
Everybody works hard.

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:28.801
There's nobody who is really crushing it

00:01:28.801 --> 00:01:32.387
who's spending ten hours a
week working on their thing.

00:01:32.387 --> 00:01:34.859
And you have to love
what you're doing because

00:01:34.859 --> 00:01:37.159
that's the only way you're
going to keep doing it.

00:01:37.159 --> 00:01:39.232
The only way you're going
to deal with all of the crap

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:42.477
of learning your craft
and all the rejection

00:01:42.477 --> 00:01:44.840
and all the failure and all
the things that don't work out

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.767
at the beginning.

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:48.248
The only thing that gets you through is

00:01:48.248 --> 00:01:50.001
you actually love the process.

00:01:50.001 --> 00:01:51.996
You love the work so it
doesn't feel like work.

00:01:51.996 --> 00:01:54.749
It's one of the most
repeated piece of advice

00:01:54.749 --> 00:01:56.676
that comes over and over
and over and over again

00:01:56.676 --> 00:01:57.716
on this channel.

00:01:57.716 --> 00:02:00.274
And so if you want to become
world class at something,

00:02:00.274 --> 00:02:03.996
you want to be the Michael
Jordan of your industry,

00:02:03.996 --> 00:02:05.645
then you have to put in the work to get

00:02:05.645 --> 00:02:07.706
really really really really good.

00:02:07.706 --> 00:02:09.790
And yes you're working smart,

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:11.880
but you have to work hard as well.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:14.798
And so a quick story with
Alex from Toronto Dance Salsa

00:02:14.798 --> 00:02:16.454
who I hired to help me run the business

00:02:16.454 --> 00:02:18.608
and he's also an instructor here.

00:02:18.608 --> 00:02:20.197
And recently we made a video where

00:02:20.197 --> 00:02:23.321
we were talking about him wanting to be

00:02:23.321 --> 00:02:25.570
the best instructor in Canada at salsa

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:27.612
and he was trying to
figure out his schedule.

00:02:27.612 --> 00:02:30.499
And he wanted to go down
to one or two days a week.

00:02:30.499 --> 00:02:32.166
And I told him that,

00:02:33.158 --> 00:02:37.215
if you want to be the
best once or twice a week

00:02:37.215 --> 00:02:38.410
is not enough.

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:41.244
In your world, you could get
deals just teaching Level 6

00:02:41.244 --> 00:02:42.916
and just teaching Mondays.

00:02:42.916 --> 00:02:43.954
- That's not enough you think?

00:02:43.954 --> 00:02:46.335
- Not enough for you to get good.

00:02:46.335 --> 00:02:48.736
I'll think you'll lose it.

00:02:48.736 --> 00:02:49.569
- Really?

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:50.691
- Yeah.

00:02:50.691 --> 00:02:54.858
If you wanted to just be a
manager and just be a coach,

00:02:56.626 --> 00:02:58.186
then it's a different story.

00:02:58.186 --> 00:03:00.910
But if you want to be the best instructor,

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:05.077
doing one night a week,
is not going to be enough.

00:03:08.142 --> 00:03:10.244
- Yeah, I didn't think about that.

00:03:10.244 --> 00:03:11.695
I don't want to be mediocre.

00:03:11.695 --> 00:03:14.092
- And then if I bring
that to my own business,

00:03:14.092 --> 00:03:16.112
if I want to have more success on YouTube,

00:03:16.112 --> 00:03:17.402
I need to put in more reps.

00:03:17.402 --> 00:03:19.060
Like, I'm doing three videos a day.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:22.690
We've done over 5,000 videos
on this channel, right.

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:24.664
You better get better at something

00:03:24.664 --> 00:03:26.458
if you're doing it 5,000 times

00:03:26.458 --> 00:03:29.468
over and over and over
and over and over again.

00:03:29.468 --> 00:03:30.927
When I started working with my agency,

00:03:30.927 --> 00:03:33.660
I was considered the worst
and I became the best

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:34.593
in a couple of months.

00:03:34.593 --> 00:03:36.547
Not because I had talent or skill,

00:03:36.547 --> 00:03:40.297
it was because I was
doing three videos a day

00:03:41.566 --> 00:03:42.983
when everybody else was having a hard time

00:03:42.983 --> 00:03:45.276
trying to do one video a week.

00:03:45.276 --> 00:03:46.109
Right?

00:03:46.109 --> 00:03:47.650
You're just going to get better faster

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:49.403
because you're putting in the work.

00:03:49.403 --> 00:03:51.383
And so whatever it is that
you want to get great at,

00:03:51.383 --> 00:03:53.360
and obviously there's some restrictions,

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:54.639
maybe you have a full time job,

00:03:54.639 --> 00:03:55.725
you know maybe you can't dedicate

00:03:55.725 --> 00:03:57.565
100% of your time to it yet,

00:03:57.565 --> 00:03:58.976
it's understandable but you need

00:03:58.976 --> 00:04:00.901
to work everyday on your craft.

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:02.781
And you need to get better
and better and better

00:04:02.781 --> 00:04:05.053
and better and better consistently

00:04:05.053 --> 00:04:06.951
Michael Jordan became Michael Jordan

00:04:06.951 --> 00:04:08.965
because of all the practice that he did.

00:04:08.965 --> 00:04:10.185
Did he have natural talent?

00:04:10.185 --> 00:04:13.167
Yes, but he worked and
he worked and he worked.

00:04:13.167 --> 00:04:15.252
And if you just write people off,

00:04:15.252 --> 00:04:17.443
you look at anybody who's
at the top of their field

00:04:17.443 --> 00:04:18.610
and you say well they're there because

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:20.885
they're naturally gifted.

00:04:20.885 --> 00:04:23.370
If that's the reasoning
for why they're successful,

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:26.554
and why you aren't more
successful, you're going to lose.

00:04:26.554 --> 00:04:29.986
Don't disrespect the amount
of effort and hard work

00:04:29.986 --> 00:04:31.352
that they are putting in.

00:04:31.352 --> 00:04:32.866
Don't disrespect the amount of hard work

00:04:32.866 --> 00:04:36.012
Michael Jordan put into
becoming Michael Jordan.

00:04:36.012 --> 00:04:39.084
Because if you just chalk
it up to natural talent,

00:04:39.084 --> 00:04:42.378
you're going to lose at whatever
it is that you're doing.

00:04:42.378 --> 00:04:46.045
Hard work almost always
beats natural talent

00:04:46.884 --> 00:04:48.555
in almost any field.

00:04:48.555 --> 00:04:52.509
And that sucks because
it's a lot of hard work,

00:04:52.509 --> 00:04:55.192
but it's also great in
that anybody can win.

00:04:55.192 --> 00:04:57.758
Like if you badly want to
win at what you're doing,

00:04:57.758 --> 00:04:59.999
as an entrepreneur, as
an actor, as a singer,

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:01.485
as a guitarist, whatever it is,

00:05:01.485 --> 00:05:03.904
if you badly want to win, you can.

00:05:03.904 --> 00:05:06.796
You just have to pay
the price of hard work.

00:05:06.796 --> 00:05:08.664
So the question of the
day today is I'm curious,

00:05:08.664 --> 00:05:11.080
are you working hard enough on the thing

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:13.377
that you say you want to be great at?

00:05:13.377 --> 00:05:16.473
Are you really putting in
enough work to become the best?

00:05:16.473 --> 00:05:17.493
I'd love to hear from you.

00:05:17.493 --> 00:05:19.306
Leave your thoughts down
in the comments below.

00:05:19.306 --> 00:05:21.210
I also want to give a
quick shoutout to Boaz.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.370
Boaz thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:25.767
Your One Word, I appreciate the support.

00:05:25.767 --> 00:05:27.279
And I hope you enjoy the read.

00:05:27.279 --> 00:05:28.574
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:05:28.574 --> 00:05:29.726
I believe in you.

00:05:29.726 --> 00:05:31.658
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:05:31.658 --> 00:05:33.662
and whatever your one word is.

00:05:33.662 --> 00:05:36.515
Much love and I'll see you
guys again tomorrow morning

00:05:36.515 --> 00:05:39.482
for another shot of entspresso.

00:05:39.482 --> 00:05:41.829
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:41.829 --> 00:05:45.246
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:05:48.564 --> 00:05:51.471
- Being in a band you have to
constantly reinvent yourself.

00:05:51.471 --> 00:05:54.526
You have to constantly be reminded

00:05:54.526 --> 00:05:56.721
how there's someone better than you.

00:05:56.721 --> 00:05:58.388
Every other weekend.

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:01.965
You're constantly reminded of how

00:06:01.965 --> 00:06:04.181
you have nothing without your fans.

00:06:04.181 --> 00:06:06.928
So you have to take into
account what they're thinking

00:06:06.928 --> 00:06:09.069
and what they're interested in.

00:06:09.069 --> 00:06:10.213
And all those things matter.

00:06:10.213 --> 00:06:12.117
But it doesn't matter what art you do.

00:06:12.117 --> 00:06:13.354
It doesn't matter if it's making an album

00:06:13.354 --> 00:06:14.774
or a movie or a book or whatever.

00:06:14.774 --> 00:06:18.046
You have to think, thinking
about all those types of things,

00:06:18.046 --> 00:06:19.440
the hard work involved.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:22.940
If you want to have like a casual life and

00:06:24.461 --> 00:06:25.294
you don't want to be in a band.

00:06:25.294 --> 00:06:26.491
I mean, you never sleep.

00:06:26.491 --> 00:06:28.862
It's really really hard work.

00:06:28.862 --> 00:06:30.650
And you're exhausted all the time.

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:32.020
And you're almost always sick.

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:33.553
And you're fighting with
your business partners

00:06:33.553 --> 00:06:34.865
all day long.

00:06:34.865 --> 00:06:37.459
And it's just how it is.

00:06:37.459 --> 00:06:39.856
But I have a very very strong work ethic

00:06:39.856 --> 00:06:42.072
because I had nothing when I was a kid.

00:06:42.072 --> 00:06:43.037
Nothing.

00:06:43.037 --> 00:06:45.313
I had my first job when I was 13.

00:06:45.313 --> 00:06:47.730
I had two jobs when I was 16.

00:06:48.926 --> 00:06:51.020
But I think a lot of it is probably

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:53.580
because I'm extraordinarily fearful

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:56.731
about having to do what
someone tells me to do.

00:06:56.731 --> 00:06:58.880
So I'd rather be doing everything

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:00.794
because at least no one's
telling me to do that.

00:07:00.794 --> 00:07:02.700
- You literally are, for
many of us in this room

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:05.010
and watching, movie wise,

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:07.151
you are the soundtrack of our lives.

00:07:07.151 --> 00:07:09.526
So much of your stuff is
obviously well known to your point

00:07:09.526 --> 00:07:11.114
and some stuff maybe not as well known,

00:07:11.114 --> 00:07:11.947
but how do you know?

00:07:11.947 --> 00:07:12.991
Is there something inside of you?

00:07:12.991 --> 00:07:16.158
How do you know when you get it right?

00:07:17.615 --> 00:07:18.947
Do you know when you get it right?

00:07:18.947 --> 00:07:20.131
- Very very rarely.

00:07:20.131 --> 00:07:22.267
You hope you've gotten 90% of it

00:07:22.267 --> 00:07:24.625
or as close to it as you can.

00:07:24.625 --> 00:07:26.343
But at least with me, and
I think with most writers

00:07:26.343 --> 00:07:29.594
of any kind, you really
don't say eureka, this is it.

00:07:29.594 --> 00:07:31.705
It's work on this, come back the next week

00:07:31.705 --> 00:07:35.353
and reshape it and do it like
a sculp-- keep honing away at.

00:07:35.353 --> 00:07:37.929
I'm not so brilliant that I
can sit down and write a melody

00:07:37.929 --> 00:07:42.284
or a theme or a whole
scene or a whole work,

00:07:42.284 --> 00:07:44.042
as Mozart might have done, we're told,

00:07:44.042 --> 00:07:48.304
dashing it off like a letter
and the grammar's perfect.

00:07:48.304 --> 00:07:51.965
Writing music it's very very hard work.

00:07:51.965 --> 00:07:55.206
And for orchestra particularly,

00:07:55.206 --> 00:07:57.276
so it's a labor intensive thing.

00:07:57.276 --> 00:07:59.600
I have to be in the
room alone all the time

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:02.517
because that's the life that it is.

00:08:04.121 --> 00:08:06.263
- It's hard work and it's lonely work.

00:08:06.263 --> 00:08:07.414
- It's hard work, it's lonely work,

00:08:07.414 --> 00:08:10.187
it's labor intensive, I
still use a pencil and paper.

00:08:10.187 --> 00:08:11.100
I don't have a computer.

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:12.092
- You're old school.

00:08:12.092 --> 00:08:15.337
- Old school, I've been
so busy fortunately

00:08:15.337 --> 00:08:18.385
that I haven't been able
to go back and retool.

00:08:18.385 --> 00:08:20.336
When I was studying music,
there were no computers.

00:08:20.336 --> 00:08:21.194
We didn't have it.

00:08:21.194 --> 00:08:24.016
- The secret to success,

00:08:24.016 --> 00:08:26.924
there's a couple of elements
that are important in success.

00:08:26.924 --> 00:08:30.454
First of all, it's your
own level of expectation.

00:08:30.454 --> 00:08:32.178
You also have to learn to be happy

00:08:32.178 --> 00:08:34.150
with what you achieve sometimes.

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:36.582
It's impossible in life to always achieve

00:08:36.582 --> 00:08:38.480
exactly what you have in
the back of your head.

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:40.253
So you need to learn also to be

00:08:40.253 --> 00:08:42.006
happy with what you achieved.

00:08:42.006 --> 00:08:46.173
Even if it's only half of
what you had in mind at first.

00:08:47.737 --> 00:08:49.547
I like a quote of John Lennon,

00:08:49.547 --> 00:08:52.252
life's what's happening
to you when you're busy

00:08:52.252 --> 00:08:53.693
making other plans.

00:08:53.693 --> 00:08:55.949
And that is what I keep
telling my wife as well.

00:08:55.949 --> 00:08:57.478
And a lot of people around me.

00:08:57.478 --> 00:08:58.828
You always expect something and then

00:08:58.828 --> 00:09:00.177
something along the way comes,

00:09:00.177 --> 00:09:02.695
and then you have to
alter your path again.

00:09:02.695 --> 00:09:04.414
And if you can learn to live with that,

00:09:04.414 --> 00:09:06.057
if you can be practical like that,

00:09:06.057 --> 00:09:08.002
then success is more easy, maybe.

00:09:08.002 --> 00:09:09.637
It's good to have a plan.

00:09:09.637 --> 00:09:11.810
But it's also good, if
you're working really hard

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:13.732
and you're walking up against a door,

00:09:13.732 --> 00:09:15.346
and you can't go through that door,

00:09:15.346 --> 00:09:18.056
then you just find a back door.

00:09:18.056 --> 00:09:19.722
Just find your way around it.

00:09:19.722 --> 00:09:21.145
And that's just the way that life is.

00:09:21.145 --> 00:09:24.447
Sometimes you cannot get
exactly what you want

00:09:24.447 --> 00:09:26.583
or what you had in the back of your mind.

00:09:26.583 --> 00:09:28.203
Yes it's very important that you have

00:09:28.203 --> 00:09:29.574
to have a good work ethic.

00:09:29.574 --> 00:09:31.570
Nobody gets anywhere without hard work.

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:33.654
And you'll have good and bad days.

00:09:33.654 --> 00:09:35.849
Even myself as a producer,

00:09:35.849 --> 00:09:39.093
I run into disappointments
almost on a daily basis

00:09:39.093 --> 00:09:41.165
because I try to work with artists that

00:09:41.165 --> 00:09:43.929
on the last moment pull back their song or

00:09:43.929 --> 00:09:45.108
you know you don't see that.

00:09:45.108 --> 00:09:46.298
You don't read that in the news.

00:09:46.298 --> 00:09:47.459
But it's the fact of the matter.

00:09:47.459 --> 00:09:49.872
And I think all artists have
to deal with stuff like that.

00:09:49.872 --> 00:09:51.331
You don't get the set times you want.

00:09:51.331 --> 00:09:52.734
You don't get the billing you want.

00:09:52.734 --> 00:09:55.017
You don't get the hotel
room that you requested.

00:09:55.017 --> 00:09:56.275
It's something you have to deal with

00:09:56.275 --> 00:09:58.992
and it defines your
character how easy you are

00:09:58.992 --> 00:10:00.674
to deal with stuff like that.

00:10:00.674 --> 00:10:03.782
You know life is a rollercoaster
ride for everybody.

00:10:03.782 --> 00:10:05.483
It has its ups and its downs.

00:10:05.483 --> 00:10:06.893
But if everything goes well,

00:10:06.893 --> 00:10:08.419
you'll have more ups than downs.

00:10:08.419 --> 00:10:09.859
And you'll remember the ups more than

00:10:09.859 --> 00:10:11.171
you'll remember the downs.

00:10:11.171 --> 00:10:12.118
But it's a fact of the matter,

00:10:12.118 --> 00:10:14.538
everybody no matter if
you're a big artist,

00:10:14.538 --> 00:10:16.767
a successful artist or a
successful businessman,

00:10:16.767 --> 00:10:18.529
everybody works hard to get somewhere.

